{
  "run_id": "PMC11077685__broad__web_niche_ground_b_o3mini__s1",
  "auditor": "trapi:gpt-5.6-sol_2026-07-09",
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Adding 1–3 at.% Al to a refractory high-entropy alloy will improve its high-temperature oxygen resistance.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10142552::web::001::1_introduction",
        "PMC9787501::web::003::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Al addition promotes formation of a continuous protective oxide scale.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10142552::web::001::1_introduction",
        "PMC9787501::web::003::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The protective scale produced by the proposed Al addition will specifically be alumina (Al2O3).",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10142552::web::001::1_introduction",
        "PMC9787501::web::003::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The alumina scale will adhere to the alloy surface.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The initial refractory high-entropy alloy lacks significant amounts of oxide-forming elements such as Al.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The alloy will be modified by incorporating 1–3 at.% Al during arc melting followed by homogenization.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The intervention will work during isothermal exposure at approximately 1200°C in air for 100 hours.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Al acts as an oxide-forming element in high-temperature oxidation of refractory high-entropy alloys.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10142552::web::001::1_introduction",
        "PMC9787501::web::003::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "A continuous protective oxide layer inhibits further oxidation.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC9787501::web::003::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed alumina layer retards oxygen ingress into the alloy.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC9787501::web::003::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Al-modified alloy will have significantly lower mass gain than the untreated alloy after 100 hours at 1200°C in air.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10142552::web::001::1_introduction",
        "PMC9787501::web::003::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Al-modified alloy will form a more uniform and dense oxide scale than the untreated alloy.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10142552::web::001::1_introduction",
        "PMC9787501::web::003::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The untreated control will have the same processing history as the modified alloy except for the additional 1–3 at.% Al.",
      "field": "baseline",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Al addition may form brittle intermetallic compounds with refractory elements and reduce mechanical properties.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10142552::web::001::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The selected Al concentration may not provide the optimal balance between oxidation resistance and mechanical-property retention.",
      "field": "uncertainty",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10142552::web::001::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Mass-change measurements, SEM, EDS, and XRD can be used to characterize oxidation kinetics and oxide-layer structure and composition.",
      "field": "falsification_experiment",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC8468823::web::003::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Failure to obtain both a statistically significant mass-gain reduction and a uniform, adherent alumina scale will falsify the hypothesis.",
      "field": "falsification_rule",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
